Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||11:41 AM||||Ok...the steering wheel moves to the left.  I can move it a good 3-4 inches.  Its like tilt steering only side to side.  What do I need to do.<P>Thanks <P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-09-2000||01:36 PM||||If it's the normal steering column problem, you need to tear the whole top of the column apart and fix 4 screws.<P>It's also posible the tilt hinges are broken. hard to say w/o seeing it.<P>You won't know untill you strip the column down pretty good.<P>easier for most people to get another column than fix these.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||05-09-2000||09:40 PM||||It takes like 20 minutes to fix if its loose and nothing is broken. But you need the proper tools. But they are cheap ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-10-2000||10:23 AM||||20 minutes? Did you only do 2 of the screws?<P>I have the tools, and I used to do allot of this stuff for a living. It still takes me at an hour, usually longer, to get those 4 screws fixed. All 4 need to be taken out, cleaned, and locktight applied. Otherwise the thing will likely come loose again, or worse something can break.<P>I also check and repair/replace the ignition lock and gears while it's apart. They always need at least cleaning and greasing. I use either "white" grease or "lubriplate" distributor grease on them. Any light grease that won't run or freeze works.||||reg||1
